{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779232072,"nonce":"lJgmkpGOHDTuJZpE3QOg6H4YASA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCyHhRA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/143","origin":"github"},"title":"Install pre-commit hooks on salmon's workspace clone (make lint never run)","message":"## Problem\n\nOn salmon, the workspace clone (`/home/field/project11`) is missing its pre-commit hook: `/home/field/project11/.git/hooks/pre-commit` does not exist. `make lint` has never been run on this host, so the workspace's `.pre-commit-config.yaml` was never wired up.\n\nDocumented in the [2026-05-19 deployment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135) salmon log §\"Issues encountered\" item 1.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml` includes `no-commit-to-branch` for `main`/`jazzy`/`rolling` plus the other workspace lint set. Today's field commit `236f2d7` (the `git_bug_setup.sh` rewrite) landed on `main` without any of those checks firing — field-mode allows the branch commit, but the other hooks (formatting, secrets-detection, etc.) should still have run and didn't.\n\nThis isn't load-bearing today (the commit was simple and reviewed inline), but **field-mode hosts will edit more invasive things in the future** — having no pre-commit safety net means a typo or accidentally-committed secret lands without local notice.\n\n## Immediate fix\n\nRun `make lint` on salmon's workspace clone (installs pre-commit and runs it once). This is the canonical onboarding step that was missed when salmon was set up. From the workspace root on salmon:\n\n```bash\nmake lint\n```\n\nPer workspace conventions, `make lint` auto-installs pre-commit + the `.venv`. After it completes, `.git/hooks/pre-commit` will exist and subsequent commits will run the full hook suite.\n\n## Verify\n\nAfter running `make lint`, confirm:\n\n```bash\nls -l .git/hooks/pre-commit            # should exist, executable\npre-commit run --all-files             # smoke-test\n```\n\n## Longer-term consideration (out of scope here)\n\nWhether `make sync` / `setup.bash` should detect missing hooks and auto-install them is a separate workspace-repo concern. File there if we want to make this self-healing — but operationally, just running `make lint` on salmon closes today's gap.\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}